ables_set" id="b15"><comment pinned="false" h="300" w="380">YOUR SETTINGS: change the numbers in this block before you run the bot.&#10;INITIAL STAKE = your stake. STOP LOSS and TAKE PROFIT = session limits in dollars. MARTINGALE = stake multiplier after a loss. OVER DIGIT / UNDER DIGIT = the digits traded (5 and 5).&#10;CYCLE: the bot trades Over 5, then Under 5, then Over 5, then Under 5 and so on. CYCLE SIDE = 0 starts with Over 5, 1 starts with Under 5.&#10;RECOVERY: a loss on Under 5 recovers with Over 5. If that loses it recovers with Under 5, then Over 5 again, and keeps switching until a trade wins. A loss on Over 5 recovers with Under 5 and switches the same way. The stake is multiplied by MARTINGALE after each loss. MAX RECOVERY = the most recovery trades it makes before it goes back to the cycle (raise it to keep recovering for longer).&#10;RESTART AT OVER = 1 starts the cycle again at Over 5 after a recovery. Set it to 0 to carry on with the next side in the cycle instead.&#10;Leave SIDE, RECOVERY SIDE and LOSS COUNT as they are.</comment><field name="VAR" id="v_INITIAL_STAKE">INITIAL STAKE</field><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_number" id="b1"><field name="NUM">0.5</field></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b14"><field name="VAR" id="v_STAKE">STAKE</field><value name="VALUE"><block type="variables_get" id="b13"><field name="VAR" id="v_INITIAL_STAKE">INITIAL STAKE</field></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b16"><field name="VAR" id="v_TAKE_PROFIT">TAKE PROFIT</field><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_number" id="b2"><field name="NUM">5</field></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b17"><field name="VAR" id="v_STOP_LOSS">STOP LOSS</field><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_number" id="b3"><field name="NUM">10</field></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b18"><field name="VAR" id="v_MARTINGALE">MARTINGALE</field><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_number" id="b4"><field name="N